findings.body:
While removing the redundant `cookie.clone()` in `WryWebviewDispatcher::delete_cookie`, the message variant was also changed from `WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie` to `WebviewMessage::SetCookie`:

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1712-1722"}

The wry event loop routes these variants to different operations:

::code{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="3731-3741"}

As a result, `Webview::delete_cookie` / `WebviewWindow::delete_cookie` will now *set* the cookie instead of deleting it — the exact opposite of the intended behavior. This silently breaks cookie removal with no error, and there is no test exercising `delete_cookie` to catch it.

::callout{type="warning"}
The fix is to restore `WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie` while keeping the `cookie.into_owned()` (no clone) change.

The renamed `window_features` method has accidental whitespace changes that stray from rustfmt conventions: an extra-wide gap in `inner_size(size.width,    size.height)` (4 spaces) and a missing space after the comma in `position(position.x,position.y)`.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1322"}

These are harmless functionally but will produce noise on the next `cargo fmt` run and look like unintentional edits. Run `cargo fmt` on the file to normalize.

In the example, `created_window_count` is declared `let mut` but `AtomicUsize::fetch_add` takes `&self`, so `mut` is unnecessary and `clippy::unnecessary_mut_passed` may flag it.

::code{file="examples/api/src-tauri/src/lib.rs" lines="77-77"}

Drop the `mut`: `let created_window_count = std::sync::atomic::AtomicUsize::new(0);`.
